#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md:41
msgid ""
"Try `match &m` and check the type of captures. The pattern syntax remains "
"the same, but the captures become shared references. This is [match "
"ergonomics](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/2005-match-ergonomics.html) and "
"is often useful with `match self` when implementing methods on an enum."
msgstr ""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md:45
msgid ""
"The same effect occurs with `match &mut m`: the captures become exclusive "
"references."
msgstr ""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md:47
msgid ""
"The distinction between a capture and a constant expression can be hard to "
"spot. Try changing the `10` in the first arm to a variable, and see that it "
"subtly doesn't work. Change it to a `const` and see it working again."
msgstr ""
